matched_variant_raw.rewritten_question_text:
A small ball with mass $m=0.1\mathrm{kg}$ is thrown horizontally from point $O$ at the right end of a horizontal platform with an initial velocity $v_0$. After leaving the platform, the ball falls tangentially into a vertical smooth circular track $ABC$ at point $A$ and just passes through the highest point $C$ along the track. The shape of the circular track $ABC$ is a circle with radius $R=2.5\mathrm{m}$ from which a $127^{\circ}$ arc at the upper left corner has been removed. $CB$ is its vertical diameter ($\sin53^{\circ}=0.8$, $\cos53^{\circ}=0.6$, gravitational acceleration $g=10\mathrm{m}/\mathrm{s}^{2}$, and air resistance is negligible). Find:
1. the magnitude of the velocity $v_C$ of the small ball as it passes through point $C$;
2. the magnitude of the supporting force exerted by the track on the small ball when it reaches the lowest point $B$ of the track;
3. the vertical height $H$ from point $O$ to point $A$.

